# AuditLogging

**Status:** Draft — founder review required
**Phase:** 7 — Operations

## Purpose

Defines what gets logged, where, and why — the audit trail that makes every
"never silently" rule from earlier phases actually checkable rather than
just promised. Backed by the `audit_log` table defined in
`DatabaseSchema.md`.

## What Gets Logged

- **Every Grant Hunter run** — sources checked, new listings found,
  eligible/ineligible counts with reasons, scored counts, drafts prepared,
  any errors — including zero-result runs (per the "silence is not
  acceptable" rule in `GrantHunter-Agent.md`)
- **Every eligibility determination** — not just the eligible ones; ruled-
  out opportunities are logged with reason, per `EligibilityEngine.md`
- **Every founder override** — of an eligibility call, a score, or a draft
  decision — feeds `ContinuousLearning.md`
- **Every source allow-list change** — addition, removal, activation,
  suspension of anything in `FundingOrganizations.md` — who approved it and
  when (Tier 3 actions are logged even though they're founder-approved,
  since the trail matters for later review)
- **Truth Standard incidents** — any fabrication or false-success report
  from any agent, logged the same way BAEOS already tracks its documented
  agent fabrication incidents

## What Doesn't Get Logged Here

- Routine successful reads (checking a score, viewing a draft) — this is an
  audit trail for actions and decisions, not a full access log

## Digest Format (Grant Hunter runs specifically)

Each run produces a human-readable digest, not just raw log rows — this is
what `StandardOperatingProcedures.md`'s weekly routine actually reads.
Format: sources checked / new found / eligible / scored / drafted / errors,
in that order, every time, so digests are scannable at a glance across
weeks.

